/T (The data come from the files Train_Arabic_Digit.txt and Test_Arabic_Digit.txt. Each utterance is a sequence of frames, and each frame is a vector of 13 Mel-frequency cepstral coefficients \(MFCCs\); utterances are separated by blank lines. The training file contains 6,600 utterances \(660 per digit\) and the test file 2,200 utterances \(220 per digit\). Utterance lengths range from 4 to 93 frames with a mean of 39.9. Class labels are assigned from the position of each utterance, because the files list the digits in consecutive equal-sized block.)
