/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 170 0 R
/T (Five of the six vanilla RNN configurations reached the 100-epoch cap without satisfying the convergence criterion, and their average training loss is noisy rather than smoothly decreasing. The LSTM and GRU models converged in 19 to 67 epochs and reached much smaller final training losses \(mostly between 0.0005 and 0.01, against 0.04 to 0.15 for the RNN models\). Convergence under this criterion is not by itself a measure of quality, but here the models that converged were also the ones that generalized best. )
/E (Five of the six vanilla RNN configurations reached the 100-epoch cap without satisfying the convergence criterion, and their average training loss is noisy rather than smoothly decreasing. The LSTM and GRU models converged in 19 to 67 epochs and reached much smaller final training losses \(mostly between 0.0005 and 0.01, against 0.04 to 0.15 for the RNN models\). Convergence under this criterion is not by itself a measure of quality, but here the models that converged were also the ones that generalized best. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
