>>
endobj
792 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 177 0 R
/E (This experiment compared RNN, LSTM and GRU classifiers for spoken Arabic digits on padded and packed MFCC sequences. Gated cells clearly outperformed the vanilla RNN: the average test accuracy was 95.80% for GRU, 95.20% for LSTM and 90.97% for RNN, and almost all gated models converged within the epoch limit while five of six RNN models did not. The best baseline by validation accuracy was a two-layer GRU with 32 hidden units \(99.55% validation, 96.27% test\). In the bonus part, bidirectional processing and attention pooling improved the test accuracy of every baseline, with the bidirectional two-layer GRU selected as the best overall model by validation accuracy \(99.70% validation, 97.55% test\). The gradient diagnostics support these findings by showing erratic, spiking gradient norms for the vanilla RNN and smooth ones for LSTM and GRU. The persistent gap between near-perfect training accuracy and 94% to 98% test accuracy suggests that regularization or data augmentation, and repeated runs with several seeds, would be the next steps for a more reliable comparison. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
